                    <occupation>Stationer and bookseller</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>James Wilmott and Robert Hill, stationers and booksellers 50 High-st
                            Borough trading as Wilmott and Hill from 1801 to 1812 (bbti). The two
                            Hills are coded to Thomas Hill in the GD website, but look closely at
                            the syntax. Godwin would have had to cross London Bridge to make these
                            calls. The next instances of Wilmot are all at Walking Stewart's, so
                            quite likely to have been a different Wilmot </p></note>
